  "source_assessment": "No patch or live-source change covers this. MOSNonReentrant.cpp (upstream code, untouched by 0002 and 0038 in the relevant analysis) adds a calls-external to external-calling edge, so main, which has external linkage and makes indirect calls, is never norecurse and MOSFrameLowering::usesStaticStack keeps its frame on the soft stack. platforms/snes*/link.ld and the installed link.ld (sha256 9eb48681...) set __stack = 0x2000 in the ram region shared with .bss/.noinit and reserve or assert nothing. No upstream llvm-mos-sdk platform script reserves or asserts a soft-stack size.",
  "binary_assessment": "The installed clang-23 254624ba..., lld c89b04cb..., llc cf5355d3... and mos-snes.cfg f12c5b6a... are the report's identities and reproduce its four ROM hashes byte for byte. Upstream llc 321-00 (2f5c1768..., equals frozen-llc.sha256, upstream 06bc967d2668) and unpatched upstream clang 742d554b (b48000f5..., manifest unpatched, empty tracked diff) fail the same way, so no downstream patch is involved.",
  "decision": "New canonical record for the SNES soft-stack/static-data collision. mos-native-width-pressure-sets only recorded the sighting; its pressure-set change is not involved, since every llc variant and plain mosw65816 fail. reentrant-attribute-contract concerns the frontend reentrant attribute contract, not a resource overlap. The rdiff fix e3bb5a62 is an earlier, unrecorded instance of the same platform mechanism, now covered here.",
