 "mitigation_observation": {
  "date": "2026-10-01",
  "status": "demo mitigated; defect record open (platform guard is separate work)",
  "summary": "examples/snes/dither.c keeps its 2304 B frame buffer in high WRAM ($7E:2000) behind the WRAM data port instead of low WRAM. Static data now ends at $16AE, leaving 2386 B to __stack (was 82 B). The gate passes (0x80C4) at -O2 and -O3 in default, +mos-a16 and +mos-a16,+mos-xy16 on bsnes-jg, and on MAME for all six. Measured soft-stack depth: 279/286/286 B at -O2 and 313/353/356 B at -O3 (default/a16/xy16), so at least 2030 B stays untouched. -O2 master clocks fall (loop per frame -19.7% default, -26.2% a16, -34.2% a16xy16). The corpus slice object is byte-identical; -verify-machineinstrs is clean at -O2/-O3 (default, a16); the picture is pixel-identical at equal iteration count. Far pointers were rejected because they fail to legalize in default mosw65816.",
  "baseline_replay": "reproduce.sh gate now builds the fixed examples/snes/dither.c; the red baseline replays only by running reproduce.sh from a checkout of origin/main 85f7972a (baseline.input and baseline.log are unchanged).",
